From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:43:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] sessions: a busy parent gets its killed-subagent
 notice once its turn ends (self-heal desktop-ac1b365935)

The startup orphan reap tells a parent chat when a restart killed its subagent mid-work, inline and once. A parent
mid-turn refuses the row (SessionTurnLeaseLostError); reap_notices logged a WARNING with a traceback and dropped the
notice for good, and nothing looked at the closed child again.

- reap_notices: a busy parent (turn lease, or compression closing its tip) is one INFO line 'parent busy, will
  retry', no traceback. Unexpected errors keep WARNING + traceback.
- retry_pending_killed_notices(db): re-offers the notice for each child closed by startup_orphan_reap in the last
  24 h (last active role tool/user) whose parent lineage lacks subagent-killed:<child>. notice_id dedup makes repeats
  a read-only no-op. Runs every kanban-unloaded sweeper pass, before guarantee_pass so the same tick can wake the
  parent. A parent still busy 30 min after the reap logs ONE WARNING per child (the real-failure line).

Why: each notice writer handled 'chat busy' itself; the kanban writers retry (kanban-e5babca565), this one did not.
Not caught: the restart test covered only an idle parent.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_session_outcome_restarts.py 3 new tests red before (WARNING at reap_notices.py:58,
no retry), 8/8 green after; 9/9 mutants of the new conditions killed; 188 tests across restarts, kanban_unloaded,
kanban_remote_wake, notice_guarantee, session_outcome, split_module_imports pass. Retry scan: ~10 ms on the hub's
19k-row sessions table.
